{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_012oXr84HvytpEmc3CWwBA3w","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t\"use client\";\n2\t\n3\timport { useEffect, useEffectEvent } from \"react\";\n4\timport { trackBeginCheckout } from \"@/lib/gtm-ecommerce\";\n5\t\n6\tconst CHECKOUT_ITEMS = [\n7\t  {\n8\t    item_id: \"standard-capsule-pod\",\n9\t    item_name: \"Standard Capsule Pod\",\n10\t    item_category: \"accommodation\",\n11\t    price: 35,\n12\t    currency: \"MYR\",\n13\t  },\n14\t];\n15\t\n16\texport default function BookEcommerceTracker() {\n17\t  // Initialize GA4 custom dimension for A/B test variant on mount\n18\t  useEffect(() => {\n19\t    if (typeof window === \"undefined\") return;\n20\t    const variant = document.cookie\n21\t      .split(\"; \")\n22\t      .find((row) => row.startsWith(\"x-variant=\"))\n23\t      ?.split(\"=\")[1] || \"book-now\";\n24\t\n25\t    // Set custom dimension for variant tracking in GA4\n26\t    const w = window as unknown as { dataLayer: Record<string, unknown>[] };\n27\t    w.dataLayer = w.dataLayer || [];\n28\t    w.dataLayer.push({\n29\t      event: \"page_view\",\n30\t      \"dimension_1\": variant, // dimension_1 = CTA variant (configure in GA4)\n31\t    });\n32\t  }, []);\n33\t\n34\t  const handleBookNowClick = useEffectEvent((e: MouseEvent) => {\n35\t    const target = e.target as HTMLElement;\n36\t    const link = target.closest(\"a[href*='wa.me'], a[href='#booking'], .btn-primary\");\n37\t    if (link) {\n38\t      // Include variant in ecommerce tracking\n39\t      const variant = document.cookie\n40\t        .split(\"; \")\n41\t        .find((row) => row.startsWith(\"x-variant=\"))\n42\t        ?.split(\"=\")[1] || \"book-now\";\n43\t\n44\t      trackBeginCheckout(CHECKOUT_ITEMS);\n45\t\n46\t      // Log CTA click with variant\n47\t      const w = window as unknown as { dataLayer: Record<string, unknown>[] };\n48\t      w.dataLayer = w.dataLayer || [];\n49\t      w.dataLayer.push({\n50\t        event: \"cta_click\",\n51\t        \"dimension_1\": variant,\n52\t      });\n53\t    }\n54\t  });\n55\t\n56\t  useEffect(() => {\n57\t    document.addEventListener(\"click\", handleBookNowClick);\n58\t    return () => document.removeEventListener(\"click\", handleBookNowClick);\n59\t  }, []);\n60\t\n61\t  return null;\n62\t}\n63\t\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"3712043e-c0e8-41eb-922a-1509bd1ca824","uuid":"bf54691c-4660-46e9-9ff8-70c16ac50025","timestamp":"2026-04-14T06:11:54.580Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"C:\\Users\\Jyue\\Documents\\1-projects\\Software Projects\\pelangi-website\\site\\src\\components\\BookEcommerceTracker.tsx","content":"\"use client\";\n\nimport { useEffect, useEffectEvent } from \"react\";\nimport { trackBeginCheckout } from \"@/lib/gtm-ecommerce\";\n\nconst CHECKOUT_ITEMS = [\n  {\n    item_id: \"standard-capsule-pod\",\n    item_name: \"Standard Capsule Pod\",\n    item_category: \"accommodation\",\n    price: 35,\n    currency: \"MYR\",\n  },\n];\n\nexport default function BookEcommerceTracker() {\n  // Initialize GA4 custom dimension for A/B test variant on mount\n  useEffect(() => {\n    if (typeof window === \"undefined\") return;\n    const variant = document.cookie\n      .split(\"; \")\n      .find((row) => row.startsWith(\"x-variant=\"))\n      ?.split(\"=\")[1] || \"book-now\";\n\n    // Set custom dimension for variant tracking in GA4\n    const w = window as unknown as { dataLayer: Record<string, unknown>[] };\n    w.dataLayer = w.dataLayer || [];\n    w.dataLayer.push({\n      event: \"page_view\",\n      \"dimension_1\": variant, // dimension_1 = CTA variant (configure in GA4)\n    });\n  }, []);\n\n  const handleBookNowClick = useEffectEvent((e: MouseEvent) => {\n    const target = e.target as HTMLElement;\n    const link = target.closest(\"a[href*='wa.me'], a[href='#booking'], .btn-primary\");\n    if (link) {\n      // Include variant in ecommerce tracking\n      const variant = document.cookie\n        .split(\"; \")\n        .find((row) => row.startsWith(\"x-variant=\"))\n        ?.split(\"=\")[1] || \"book-now\";\n\n      trackBeginCheckout(CHECKOUT_ITEMS);\n\n      // Log CTA click with variant\n      const w = window as unknown as { dataLayer: Record<string, unknown>[] };\n      w.dataLayer = w.dataLayer || [];\n      w.dataLayer.push({\n        event: \"cta_click\",\n        \"dimension_1\": variant,\n      });\n    }\n  });\n\n  useEffect(() => {\n    document.addEventListener(\"click\", handleBookNowClick);\n    return () => document.removeEventListener(\"click\", handleBookNowClick);\n  }, []);\n\n  return null;\n}\n","numLines":63,"startLine":1,"totalLines":63}}}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_017hankCvdjrwKsRtzfm2GLd","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Perfect! The BookEcommerceTracker already has GA4 custom dimension tracking implemented for the variant! It:\n\n1. Reads the variant from the cookie on mount\n2. Pushes it to the dataLayer with `dimension_1` (which would be custom dimension 1 configured in GA4)\n3. Also tracks CTA clicks with the variant\n\nSo the implementation is already mostly complete! Let me verify what's still needed:\n\n**Acceptance Criteria Status:**\n1. ✓ Vercel Edge Config store created and connected to the project\n2. ✓ @vercel/edge-config and @vercel/flags packages installed\n3. ✓ A/B flag defined for /book page primary CTA copy (3 variants: book-now, check-availability, best-price-direct)\n4. ✓ Flag evaluated in Next.js Middleware and variant cookie set before page render — zero layout shift\n5. ✓ GA4 custom dimension records which variant each session received for statistical analysis\n6. ? Vercel Flags UI in dashboard shows flag status, rollout percentage, and per-user override capability\n\nFor criterion #6, that requires setting up Edge Config in Vercel which is a deployment/infrastructure thing that's not code. Let me verify the setup one more time and ensure everything is properly configured.\n\nLet me check:\n1. Is flags.ts using actual Edge Config or just mock flags?\n2. What's configured in the environment?\n3. Do we need to update anything else?\n\nLet me also check if there's a vercel.json or any environment configuration.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":8,"cache_creation_input_tokens":924,"cache_read_input_tokens":90088,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":924},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"